      "title": "Reject invalid timestamp meanings with a domain error",
      "description": "`Timestamp.__post_init__` checks the nanosecond range but does not validate that `meaning` is a `TimeMeaning`. If a `Timestamp` is constructed with an invalid meaning, `SignalEvent` reaches this branch and accesses `self.time.meaning.value`, raising `AttributeError` instead of the documented `InvalidSignalError`. Validate the meaning before reading `.value` so malformed timestamps fail through the signal model\u2019s error contract.",
